  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466436",
      "title": "Reflecting the Auth State in the UI",
      "lectureOrder": 625,
      "videoOrder": 576,
      "sourceHash": "4947b0d2c1a00c17e36f78d5032be101dc116a909f1a80d976a9d0744ab47284",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "Male Instructor: Let's start by forwarding the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 7.83,
          "en": "to a different route once the user is locked in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 9.93,
          "en": "Now since we always want to redirect the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.93,
          "end": 11.61,
          "en": "once we authenticate it, we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.61,
          "end": 14.07,
          "en": "of course can do this in two different places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.07,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "We can either do it here and handle authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "or we do it in the component here instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "of subscribe in the success case only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "Of course, now it's up to you when you do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 27.3,
          "en": "If you prefer redirecting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.3,
          "end": 32.3,
          "en": "in the component or from inside a service, both is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.55,
          "end": 35.07,
          "en": "And if you need no data from either the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.07,
          "end": 37.32,
          "en": "or the component and you have no strong reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.32,
          "end": 39.3,
          "en": "for doing it at one place or the other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 42.12,
          "en": "it's totally up to you where you do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "Now you could argue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "that you want to keep your service a bit cleaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 49.02,
          "en": "and don't interact with the user interface in the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "So don't directly influence the user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 54.3,
          "en": "and therefore you maybe don't want to interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.3,
          "end": 55.74,
          "en": "with the router in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.74,
          "end": 57.93,
          "en": "though, I see no problem with doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "And we did it before in the course as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "Nonetheless, to mix things up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 67.523,
          "en": "I will do it in the component and I will inject the router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.7,
          "end": 73.32,
          "en": "the angular router, which is injected from @angular/router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.32,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "with the router injected in the off component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "in subscribe, but only the success case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 80.88,
          "en": "Of course, I want to use the router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.88,
          "end": 85.173,
          "en": "and navigate q/recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.68,
          "end": 89.513,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.53,
          "end": 94.53,
          "en": "This is a great example for programmatic navigation now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.53,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "where you couldn't use a link in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 99.50999999999999,
          "en": "because you want to navigate once some action is done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.50999999999999,
          "end": 101.94,
          "en": "and you don't want to navigate when a user clicks something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.94,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "but only once the user click the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "and the login is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 107.46000000000001,
          "en": "Therefore, we need to navigate from inside code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.46000000000001,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "because this is where we know once this is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "So now let's give this a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "Let's see if it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "Let's try logging in and we go to recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "Great, let's now try to create a new user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 125.01,
          "en": "So you have test 2, switch to sign up and click sign up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.01,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "And this works too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 129.72,
          "en": "So navigating works, of course, we still can go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.72,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "to authenticate because we still have it here in the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 135.57,
          "en": "And on the other hand, if we're not authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "for example, if I reload the app, then all the previous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "states lost and we are not authenticated because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "the user object doesn't exist anymore in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 146.04,
          "en": "We'll soon add something to persist it, but for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.04,
          "end": 147.24,
          "en": "that's how it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.24,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "So even if we're not locked in, we still see recipes even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "though we don't really want to be able to go there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 154.56,
          "en": "So the next step will be that we correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "reflect our current status here in the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 161.103,
          "en": "And that in this application, mostly means, in the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "In the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "If we have a look at the HTML code and the anti goal will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 170.326,
          "en": "to disable this recipes link if we are not logged",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.326,
          "end": 173.01,
          "en": "in to disable the authenticate link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 175.38,
          "en": "if we are logged in because we, well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 176.73,
          "en": "there is no sense in logging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.73,
          "end": 178.98,
          "en": "in again, if we are logged in right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "To always show the shopping list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 183.45,
          "en": "to disable the dropdown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.45,
          "end": 185.76,
          "en": "if we are not logged in because saving",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.76,
          "end": 188.94,
          "en": "and fetching data is only available if we are logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188.94,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "And to also show a logout button that allows us to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "well, log out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 194.423,
          "en": "Let me start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 194.423,
          "end": 197.43,
          "en": "with the logout button here, for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 197.43,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "I'll add a new list item here and in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 201.97,
          "en": "anchor tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 206.43,
          "en": "where I say \"logout\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 206.43,
          "end": 210.09,
          "en": "without any reference or router link set just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.09,
          "end": 212.94,
          "en": "Now, let's also add this style here to make sure we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "get a nice cursor when hovering over that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 217,
          "en": "But that's of course totally optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 217.92000000000002,
          "end": 220.89,
          "en": "Now we have that logout button here and now we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 220.89,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "need to make sure we get the current authentication status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "into the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 226.89,
          "en": "So we basically find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 226.89,
          "end": 229.82999999999998,
          "en": "out do we have a user with a valid token or not?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 229.82999999999998,
          "end": 232.07999999999998,
          "en": "And we then also need to use the information to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 232.07999999999998,
          "end": 235.32,
          "en": "update the template correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 235.32,
          "end": 238.38,
          "en": "Now for that, first of all, in the off service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 238.38,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "right now we manage our user here through a subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 244.41,
          "en": "This will inform all places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 244.41,
          "end": 248.31,
          "en": "in the application about when our user changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 248.31,
          "end": 249.54,
          "en": "And right now, even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 249.54,
          "end": 252.09,
          "en": "though we haven't implemented all the logic for that yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 252.09,
          "end": 255.03,
          "en": "let's assume that it always changes when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 255.03,
          "end": 256.74,
          "en": "the authentication status changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 256.74,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "So even if the token expires",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 258.6,
          "end": 261.57,
          "en": "the user subject will emit a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 261.57,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "which is then null because then the user is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 267.69,
          "en": "We haven't added that logic yet, but we will add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 267.69,
          "end": 271.47,
          "en": "So let's assume that the subject here is our source of truth",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 271.47,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "and therefore the header component, since it's always there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "in our application, can subscribe to that subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 281.58,
          "en": "to update correctly based on the user's status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 281.58,
          "end": 284.13,
          "en": "So in the header component \"TypeScript file\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 284.13,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "we can now inject the off service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 289.32,
          "en": "which is of type of service of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 289.32,
          "end": 292.983,
          "en": "and you need to import off service from that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 294.51,
          "end": 299.51,
          "en": "And we can then add NG OnInit by adding the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 299.58,
          "end": 302.231,
          "en": "OnInit interface here, which is also imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 302.231,
          "end": 307.05,
          "en": "from @angular core and inside of NG OnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 307.05,
          "end": 309.78,
          "en": "I want to set up a subscription to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 309.78,
          "end": 312.27,
          "en": "off service user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 312.27,
          "end": 314.43,
          "en": "So we can set up a subscription here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 314.43,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "And as you learned in the RX JS section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 318.48,
          "en": "such subscriptions should be managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 318.48,
          "end": 320.49,
          "en": "by you so that you unsubscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 320.49,
          "end": 322.29,
          "en": "If it's not required anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 322.29,
          "end": 324.87,
          "en": "For that I'll add a new private property user sub",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 324.87,
          "end": 327.36,
          "en": "which is of type subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 327.36,
          "end": 330.24,
          "en": "And subscription is imported from RX JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 330.24,
          "end": 333.96,
          "en": "So this import needs to be added to the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 333.96,
          "end": 338.31,
          "en": "And with that added, we store the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 338.31,
          "end": 341.34000000000003,
          "en": "in that user sub property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 341.34000000000003,
          "end": 345.27,
          "en": "and now also add OnDestroy here, which is also imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 345.27,
          "end": 348.81,
          "en": "from at @angular core so that we are forced to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 348.81,
          "end": 351.99,
          "en": "NGOnDestroy where we can clear that subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 351.99,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "So here I call this userSub.unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 359.34000000000003,
          "en": "The more interesting part for us of course happens inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 359.34000000000003,
          "end": 362.64,
          "en": "of subscribe here because there we get a user object and now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 362.64,
          "end": 367.41,
          "en": "as I mentioned, let's rely on the fact that this user is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 367.41,
          "end": 370.98,
          "en": "either now if we're not locked in or exists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 370.98,
          "end": 372.87,
          "en": "So if it's the user object, it's not now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 372.87,
          "end": 376.02,
          "en": "but it's a concrete object if we are locked in.",
